---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { articles } from '../lib/content';
const stories=(await articles()).filter(a=>/space|astronomy/i.test(a.category?.title||''));
---
<Layout title="Space & Astronomy | ATHENA" description="Explore the universe with ATHENA: astronomy, space exploration and documentaries.">
<section class="text-page"><p class="eyebrow">ATHENA / SPACE & ASTRONOMY</p><h1>A wider universe.</h1><p class="standfirst">Discoveries, missions and the people asking what lies beyond our world.</p>
{stories.length>0 && <section><h2>Space reporting</h2>{stories.map(a=><p><a href={'/article/'+a.slug.current+'/'}>{a.title}</a></p>)}</section>
<h2>Documentary room</h2><p>Films from the organisations exploring our universe. Archive films provide context; they are not live mission updates.</p>
<h3>Hubble: The Great Space Telescope</h3><p>NASA’s documentary traces the telescope’s scientific achievements and the human work that kept it observing.</p>
<iframe class="news-video" title="NASA Hubble documentary" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/Lo43Gq_Xe1M" loading="lazy" allowfullscreen></iframe>
<p>NASA Goddard · Archive documentary · <a href="https://plus.nasa.gov/video/hubble-the-great-space-telescope/">Watch on NASA+</a></p>
<h3>Cosmic Dawn</h3><p>Follow the assembly, testing and launch of the James Webb Space Telescope.</p><p><a href="https://www.nasa.gov/cosmicdawn/">Watch the documentary through NASA →</a></p>
</section>
</Layout>
